INT. ROOFTOP RADIO SHACK - NIGHT

A tarpaper hut on a flat roof above a laundromat. Antenna wire runs out the window like a clothesline. A ham-radio rig glows green. A desk lamp, a scatter of QSL cards, a cracked globe.

THEODORA "TEDDY" LINDGREN (16, braids, headphones around her neck) leans over the microphone, one foot tucked under her. She's been here for hours.

She presses the key.

TEDDY
CQ, CQ. This is Whiskey Two Tango Lima. Anyone out there?

Static rolls. She turns the dial. A faint voice surfaces.

VOICE (V.O.)
(over radio, crackly)
Whiskey Two Tango Lima, this is Kilo Nine Echo. I read you, three by three.

Teddy grins. She grabs the mic.

TEDDY
Kilo Nine Echo! Where are you?

VOICE (V.O.)
Outside Reykjavik. Fishing boat. You're my first contact this month.

TEDDY
Seriously? I'm on a roof in Newark.

VOICE (V.O.)
Newark. Lovely. What's your name, Newark?

TEDDY
Teddy.

VOICE (V.O.)
Teddy. I'm Gunnar.

Her smile grows. Then, from below, a door slams. Footsteps on the stairwell. A heavy knock on the roof hatch, twice.

She freezes, mic in hand. The green light flickers on her face.

TEDDY
(whispering into the mic)
Gunnar, I gotta go. My dad's home.

GUNNAR (V.O.)
Come back tomorrow?

TEDDY
Maybe.

Another knock, louder. She switches the rig off. The glow dies. She sits in the dark, hand on the dial, listening to the quiet.

Then, softly, she clicks the lamp back on and taps out three beeps on the key. Dit dit dit. Dah dah dah. Dit dit dit.

TEDDY (CONT'D)
(to herself)
See you tomorrow, Gunnar.

She grabs her headphones and heads for the door.
